cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the underlying model papers listed under references."
title: "openfoam-blood: a two-velocity phase-field clot solver for OpenFOAM 13"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/alirezakianim/openfoam-blood"
authors:
  - family-names: Kianimoqadam
    given-names: Alireza
abstract: >-
  Research code (not a validated blood-flow model): a runtime-selectable
  OpenFOAM-13 solver module for platelet-driven clot growth, poroelastic
  deformation and detachment on a planar mural geometry, with a generator
  for the pre-registered case series and the offline checks that guard it.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Čapek
        given-names: Martin
    title: "A phase-field method applied to interface tracking for blood clot formation"
    journal: "Applications of Mathematics"
    volume: 65
    issue: 4
    start: 447
    end: 481
    year: 2020
    doi: "10.21136/AM.2020.0056-19"
